        <item>
            <title>0.2.6</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2026 13:22:34 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1774037970</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Theme-driven chat typography — Chat font sizes and spacing are now controlled by your theme rather than hardcoded, so custom themes can adjust text size and layout density across all chat elements.</li>
<li>Dedicated thinking block rendering — Thinking blocks now use their own markdown renderer with independent font and color settings, separate from regular message text.</li>
<li>Taller multiline prompt field — The chat composer's multiline input now shows up to 8 visible lines (up from 5) before scrolling, giving you more room to compose longer messages.</li>
<li>Light theme polish — Adjusted pane borders, footer backgrounds, card hover borders, and chat background colors in the light theme for better contrast and consistency.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Fixed Codex chat duplicating text — The Codex stream parser was emitting the same text twice when an <code>item.completed</code> event repeated text already sent during <code>item.started</code>. Text is now deduplicated per block.</li>
<li>Fixed chat blocks stuck in streaming state — When the model finished a message without explicitly closing its content blocks, text and thinking blocks would remain incomplete. Open blocks are now finalized automatically when the message ends.</li>
<li>Fixed empty assistant messages briefly flashing — Whitespace-only text blocks (common during streaming) were incorrectly treated as visible content, causing empty message wrappers to appear and create visual gaps.</li>
<li>Fixed CloudKit sync race condition — Concurrent access to the pending saves/deletes state could cause data corruption during sync. Added proper locking to serialize access from multiple threads.</li>
<li>Fixed multiline prompt field scroll position not resetting when content shrinks back below the maximum height after deleting text.</li>
<li>Fixed multiline prompt field text layout not properly updating its frame height after content changes, which could cause clipping or extra whitespace.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
